      "text": "#RetardedTherapy \n\nThe reason I say not to be casually cruel or engage in casual cruelty and not to mock people who have done nothing to you personally and whose existence doesn't offend you is because of the simple truth that you'll rot and feel bad, I was like that once.\n\nWe had this guy flown in, terror charges and the usual and whatever, and I happened to be interior security and I had to cope with the fact that some bread loafs were moldy and he was the perfect target, so I went to him and I said that I never had sex with a woman and he's going to be my first, so I'll buy him a wig and make sure his first meal wasn't so bad and I'll even throw a juicebox or two in, but first we have to make you one... You know that sort of conversation, he wetted himself by the end of it and then I stopped, I felt pretty bad, this was textbook psychopathic behavior and I felt pretty disgusted with myself, and the worst is? He wasn't actually a terrorist, he just happened to be a drug smuggler of hashish and he was selling it off, yes, sure, it was grown by ISIS and he was giving them money, but it's not like he was one of *them*, only under the general umbrella.\n\nWe never did anything, of course, but the trip didn't feel that good after it was over, the premise is actually the same whether you're going through school or your university or your workplace, it'll just expose the fact that you're desperate to bend any people you can just because, unhealthy, psychologically speaking.",
